@Granyte, of course lowering the update rate for far away objects and removing updates for culled objects are basic optimizations that must be implemented. Those two alone will drastically reduce bandwidth consumption. To take it a step further would be having clients predict the physics interactions, which in turn would allow you to lower the update rate <em class="text-italics">exponentially</em>. You of all people making an MMO should be able to fully grasp the benefits of a system I'm proposing.<br><br>The only real question I'm asking in this thread is where should I begin looking to start implementing such a system? Would this require a new solver? Extending a current solver? Creating a new type of rigid body? etc.. If I'm going to take this task head-on I want to get started on the right foot.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=10757">KKlouzal</a> — Mon Sep 08, 2014 10:49 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
